(7485116, 1190647, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>Another excellent image Eugene. More often than not you manage to produce an image that stands out in every challenge mainly through sheer technical abilities either in-camera or post-processing or both. This is a good example of such an image, the moon has a luminescent quality that transcends the normal straightforward rendition that is normally seen. The only small problem I have with it is the white crater at about 10 oclock it is very much brighter and although it is small it  is quite prominent and somewhat unnatural with its squareish shape.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge Another excellent image Eugene. More often than not you manage to produce an image that stands out in every challenge mainly through sheer technical abilities either in-camera or post-processing or both. This is a good example of such an image, the moon has a luminescent quality that transcends the normal straightforward rendition that is normally seen. The only small problem I have with it is the white crater at about 10 oclock it is very much brighter and although it is small it  is quite prominent and somewhat unnatural with its squareish shape.', '2016-11-30 05:19:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7485118, 1190632, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>Youre right Drake theres plenty of detail there, it must have been a surprisingly bright moon given your technical details. The one thing that really detracts for me is the chromatic aberration(?), there is green halo all round it particularly evident at the top. Again, like your commenter, I have to be consistent having already commented on the bright crater at about 9 oclock on another image I think it would have benefited from a little dodging just to make it a little less obvious.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge Youre right Drake theres plenty of detail there, it must have been a surprisingly bright moon given your technical details. The one thing that really detracts for me is the chromatic aberration(?), there is green halo all round it particularly evident at the top. Again, like your commenter, I have to be consistent having already commented on the bright crater at about 9 oclock on another image I think it would have benefited from a little dodging just to make it a little less obvious.', '2016-11-30 05:27:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7485121, 1190659, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>You have every right to be pleased with your image Louis. There is good focus with plenty of detail. It must have been a very bright moon with f16 as your chosen aperture you still managed to get 1/100s, to be honest I think you could probably have made it a bit easier for yourself given the relatively flat focal plane f8 would probably have sufficed. I think you could have improved it post-processing with more contrast it is somewhat uniform tonally. Given that this is your first attempt at a moon shot it is a very good result, well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge You have every right to be pleased with your image Louis. There is good focus with plenty of detail. It must have been a very bright moon with f16 as your chosen aperture you still managed to get 1/100s, to be honest I think you could probably have made it a bit easier for yourself given the relatively flat focal plane f8 would probably have sufficed. I think you could have improved it post-processing with more contrast it is somewhat uniform tonally. Given that this is your first attempt at a moon shot it is a very good result, well done.', '2016-11-30 05:35:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7485122, 1190696, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>Simple is usually the best way to go Tracy, a straightforward shot without any clutter or distractions and you have captured the essence of the moon theres no mistaking that. Although you have the detail of the moon it all feels a little on the soft side, if you compare some of the other challenge entries you will hopefully appreciate what I mean. Theres not a lot you can do compositionally so its good that its not perfectly central but because it isnt perhaps better use of one the hotspots would have also given it a little more impact.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge Simple is usually the best way to go Tracy, a straightforward shot without any clutter or distractions and you have captured the essence of the moon theres no mistaking that. Although you have the detail of the moon it all feels a little on the soft side, if you compare some of the other challenge entries you will hopefully appreciate what I mean. Theres not a lot you can do compositionally so its good that its not perfectly central but because it isnt perhaps better use of one the hotspots would have also given it a little more impact.', '2016-11-30 05:43:02.000000', NULL, 0),
